1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,004
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:12,512
-[Julio]<i> You're not using your brain!</i>
<i>-Ouch!</i>

3
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:15,598
<i>You imbecile! Show some dignity!</i>

4
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:18,685
<i>I don't care about what people say.</i>

5
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:19,811
[shouting] <i>You are right!</i>

6
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:23,273
<i>I am the governor,</i>
<i>and I can do anything I want!</i>

7
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:26,025
[Arnaldo chuckles] <i>A lunatic escaped me.</i>

8
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:28,695
-<i>That lunatic got away!</i>
-[gunshots]

9
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:32,407
<i>If the congressman asks</i>
<i>if I've already dealt with Arthur,</i>

10
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,576
<i>-do you know what to say?</i>
<i>-You don't have to tell me.</i>

11
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:37,328
[Ivy] <i>Tomorrow, the Ardientes will wake up</i>

12
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:39,873
<i>to a living nightmare.</i>

13
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,458
-<i>This is the Senator's cut.</i>
-<i>Is this all of it?</i>

14
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:42,751
<i>That's the Senator's. Give it to him.</i>

15
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:45,545
[Ivy] <i>If the issue spreads,</i>
<i>the media will swarm you,</i>

16
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>especially because you passed</i>
<i>the Anti-Gambling Bill.</i>

17
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:49,799
[reporter] <i>But how</i>
<i>do you explain your name</i>

18
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:52,343
<i>being mentioned in the video itself?</i>

19
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:55,305
<i>Our empire is falling,</i>
<i>and I need to save it.</i>

20
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:59,851
<i>Just prove to everyone</i>
<i>that we Ardientes are good people,</i>

21
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:01,019
<i>that we are innocent.</i>

22
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:02,562
<i>But you are innocent, right?</i>

23
00:01:02,645 --> 00:01:05,273
<i>Everything they're accusing us of is true.</i>

24
00:01:05,356 --> 00:01:09,069
[Ivy] <i>The Ardiente's downfall</i>
<i>is within reach.</i>

25
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:12,238
<i>I will fix this. We will fix this.</i>

26
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:13,656
<i>I'll talk to my parents</i>

27
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:17,869
<i>and track down whoever</i>
<i>is messing with the Ardientes.</i>

28
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:21,456
<i>When I'm gone, all this will be yours.</i>

29
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:25,502
<i>You will be the king</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

30
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,962
[Diego] <i>Don't you think</i>
<i>it's time for our family to change?</i>

31
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:28,963
<i>We don't have to change anything.</i>

32
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:31,925
<i>In Ardiente, we are the rulers!</i>

33
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:33,635
<i>Raul, you moron!</i>

34
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:36,346
<i>This is all your fault!</i>

35
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:38,139
-[Raul] <i>I'll kill you!</i>
<i>-Stop it! Stop!</i>

36
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,309
[Emilia] Papa! Papa!

37
00:01:42,811 --> 00:01:45,605
Papa! [crying]

38
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:49,359
What are you looking at? Get help!

39
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:51,653
Call an ambulance! Hurry!

40
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:54,072
-Call an ambulance! Help!
-Help!

41
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:55,949
-[Arnaldo] Grandpa!
-[Emilia] Papa!

42
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:58,618
Call an ambulance! Call an ambulance!

43
00:01:58,701 --> 00:02:00,453
[Raul] Diego, call an ambulance. Hurry!

44
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:01,454
Papa!

45
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:04,165
[Emilia sobbing]

46
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:05,917
-Hello?
-Papa!

47
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,336
This is Mayor Arnaldo.
Mayor of Poblacion Ardiente.

48
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:10,463
I need an ambulance here in our mansion.

49
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,673
Pronto!

50
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:13,925
-[Emilia] Papa!
-What happened?

51
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:15,552
Papa!

52
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:18,721
[sobbing] Papa.

53
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,349
Papa!

54
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,936
[Emilia wailing]

55
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:33,945
-[shushes]
-[Tonio] Hey!

56
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:36,948
Lily… Run!

57
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,325
Mom.

58
00:02:42,287 --> 00:02:43,663
<i>Mom?</i>

59
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:46,541
[sobbing]

60
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:47,792
Mom.

61
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:49,502
Mom! Mom!

62
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:52,589
[pensive music playing]

63
00:03:05,059 --> 00:03:07,020
-[Emilia] Papa!
-[Arnaldo] Hurry! Double time!

64
00:03:07,103 --> 00:03:10,106
Papa, don't leave us!

65
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:14,027
Arnaldo, make sure
your grandfather survives!

66
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:15,612
I will. I'll go with them.

67
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:18,239
Let's go, let's go!

68
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,199
[sobs]

69
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:23,536
[siren wailing]

70
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,626
Mom, what happened to grandpa?

71
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:32,712
[tense music playing]

72
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:37,800
He and your dad had a fight.

73
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,221
Then he had a heart attack.

74
00:03:44,515 --> 00:03:47,644
Go follow your brother. He needs you.

75
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,354
Okay, Mom, Dad.

76
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:10,750
[ominous music plays]

77
00:04:11,417 --> 00:04:13,836
Ouch! Ouch! Hey! It hurts! Watch it.

78
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,047
Relax. It's me. Ouch!

79
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:17,715
What's wrong with you?

80
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:21,928
Jepoy, you're lucky I don't have a gun,
or I could've shot you on the spot.

81
00:04:22,011 --> 00:04:24,764
-I'm sorry.
-Why are you here?

82
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:30,395
Julio Ardiente's in the hospital.
He had a heart attack.

83
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:36,109
[tense music playing]

84
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,779
[doctor] I'm sorry, Mayor.
This is as far as you can go.

85
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:44,617
-Mayor.
-Doc.

86
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,119
I'll leave him in your hands.

87
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:48,246
Don't worry.
We will do everything for him.

88
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,832
Thank you.

89
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:00,675
You tried to kill him, Raul!

90
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:02,593
You monster! You tried to kill him!

91
00:05:02,677 --> 00:05:07,849
Please listen to me.
I didn't mean to, Emilia.

92
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:11,019
-I wasn't thinking straight. I just--
-Get out. Get out!

93
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:12,854
I was just hurt by what he said to me.

94
00:05:12,937 --> 00:05:14,397
-I lost it--
-Leave me alone!

95
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,982
I'd never do that to your father.

96
00:05:16,065 --> 00:05:17,650
-Hear me out first.
-Leave me alone!

97
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,360
Get out.

98
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:21,029
Get out!

99
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:24,198
[ominous music playing]

100
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:31,080
Arnaldo. How's grandpa doing?

101
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:33,249
He's in the OR now.

102
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:36,252
He's in critical condition.
He needs surgery.

103
00:05:37,253 --> 00:05:38,921
Cardiac arrest.

104
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:40,298
But it doesn't make sense.

105
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:43,801
Why did the doctor say
there could be asphyxiation involved?

106
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,804
What happened back there?

107
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:50,391
Mom said grandpa had a heart attack

108
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,018
because he and dad fought.

109
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:53,936
Yes, we heard them.

110
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,856
But why did the doctor say
asphyxiation was involved?

111
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:02,820
[sobbing]

112
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:05,907
[dramatic music playing]

113
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:12,789
Papa.

114
00:06:26,719 --> 00:06:31,140
[Julio] This is all your fault.

115
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,059
You.

116
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:37,647
You and your weaknesses as a woman.

117
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:41,526
Straighten yourself out! Understand?

118
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:48,324
[sobs]

119
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:51,869
If he dies…

120
00:06:53,329 --> 00:06:55,873
What will happen if Papa dies?

121
00:06:57,458 --> 00:07:00,086
[Ivy] <i>You're only a governor in name.</i>

122
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:03,422
I can see how you let your father
boss you around.

123
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:08,636
Maybe it's time you show them
that you can stand beside them.

124
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:13,724
Not as a woman, but as an Ardiente.

125
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:16,102
[dramatic music playing]

126
00:07:16,185 --> 00:07:19,188
[Julio] <i>Did you forget</i>
<i>that you're the governor?</i>

127
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:22,859
Getting drunk like that?
You have no self-respect!

128
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:26,195
I don't care about what people say!

129
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,822
You are right!

130
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:30,783
I am the governor,
and I can do anything I want!

131
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:33,870
Stop treating me like your puppet!

132
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:37,415
Starting now, I am in charge of my life!

133
00:07:38,749 --> 00:07:41,752
[ominous music playing]

134
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:57,059
[thinking] <i>If Papa dies,</i>
<i>I can take his place.</i>

135
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:03,107
[chuckling]

136
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:16,621
How is your grandfather?

137
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:21,125
He's in the operating room, critical.

138
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:25,046
Mom, where's Dad?

139
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:28,299
He's blaming himself for what happened.

140
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:31,344
They were arguing when
your grandfather had a heart attack.

141
00:08:31,427 --> 00:08:33,471
Was that all that happened, Mom?

142
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:36,349
I was there.

143
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:37,350
Are you doubting me?

144
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:39,685
Well, doctors found something different.

145
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:41,771
Grandpa was strangled.

146
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:44,232
What? That's outrageous.

147
00:08:44,315 --> 00:08:46,526
Your dad would never do that
to your grandfather.

148
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:52,365
Okay. Let's just wait
for the doctor's findings.

149
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:55,701
And the people should know
about what happened.

150
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:57,245
I have to call someone.

151
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:04,752
[line ringing]

152
00:09:04,835 --> 00:09:06,254
Hello?

153
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:09,382
The congressman is sick.
Cancel all his meetings.

154
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:13,177
And call some reporters
to come to the hospital.

155
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,186
So, what's your plan?

156
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:26,732
[phone ringing]

157
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:35,283
-Yes, Emilia?
-Did I wake you up?

158
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:37,493
No, it's okay. Why?

159
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,328
Papa had a heart attack.

160
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:41,664
What?

161
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:42,915
Uh… How is he?

162
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:44,542
He's very critical.

163
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:47,962
Um… Emilia, just relax.

164
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:49,714
I'll go see you.

165
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:52,383
Thank you, Ivy. You're a real friend.

166
00:09:52,466 --> 00:09:53,676
Thank you.

167
00:09:57,513 --> 00:10:00,808
It looks like Congressman
is in critical condition.

168
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:02,518
He was rushed to the hospital.

169
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:04,186
[tense music playing]

170
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:08,482
They can't keep his real condition
a secret any longer.

171
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:11,360
Do you really have to go there?

172
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:17,241
Jepoy, Emilia thinks
we're friends, remember?

173
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:23,331
That's why I need to make
her feel she can count on me

174
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:24,915
whenever she's in need.

175
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:28,919
Besides, I want to see Julio suffering.

176
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,965
Ivy, would you consider this a victory?

177
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:37,053
Well, this isn't part of my plans.

178
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:41,182
But I'd like to believe…

179
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:46,604
that this is a fitting punishment

180
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:49,607
for all the Ardientes' past sins.

181
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:54,945
Let's just call this… karma.

182
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:09,543
[Diego scoffs]

183
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:12,380
News really does travel fast.

184
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:16,634
Um… Mr. Torillo, I'm sorry
about what happened to your grandfather.

185
00:11:17,218 --> 00:11:18,302
Sorry?

186
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:22,598
Why are you apologizing?
Is it your fault he had a heart attack?

187
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:24,850
[tense music playing]

188
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,063
Fine.

189
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:33,567
Mr. Torillo, if you don't want me
to sympathize with your family,

190
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:34,860
I won't force it.

191
00:11:37,822 --> 00:11:39,240
Excuse me.

192
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:43,994
You know… I just realized.

193
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:47,373
Whenever something bad happens
to my family, you're always there.

194
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,876
Why is that?

195
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:53,838
Can you explain, Ms. Aguas?

196
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:59,468
Why are you so concerned about my family?

197
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,142
Diego?

198
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:09,061
What are you doing?

199
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:12,982
Uh, Mom, I was just asking
Ms. Aguas something.

200
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:15,734
Ivy, thank you for coming.

201
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:18,195
Of course, Emilia. How is the congressman?

202
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:19,947
He's still in the OR.

203
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,616
I hope the operation goes well.

204
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,702
And I'm hoping for the same.

205
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:26,120
Let's go to the OR.

206
00:12:26,203 --> 00:12:28,706
I want to be the first
to see him when he wakes up.

207
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,040
-Sure.
-Come.

208
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:31,333
All right.

209
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:37,673
[scoffs]

210
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:40,759
[unsettling music playing]

211
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:45,389
I'm afraid the condition
of the patient is not stable.

212
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:48,893
He needs to be transferred
to a better-equipped hospital.

213
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:53,272
He needs to undergo a triple bypass
operation as soon as possible.

214
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,399
But he's going to be okay, doc, right?

215
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:59,361
[doctor] Well, I'm not so sure.

216
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:03,073
But I know he needs
special medical attention.

217
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,742
And he needs it now.

218
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:08,621
Do everything you can, doc, to make
his transfer to Manila comfortable.

219
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:10,623
Get the elite heart surgeons.

220
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:13,042
I want him to undergo surgery
as soon as possible.

221
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:17,963
Doc, you mentioned something
about asphyxiation.

222
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:20,132
Was that the cause of his heart attack?

223
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:23,177
[unsettling music playing]

224
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:27,097
Uh… Well, I'm sorry,
but there was some confusion.

225
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:28,349
That was actually another patient.

226
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:31,685
The heart attack of the congressman
is due to stress.

227
00:13:34,104 --> 00:13:36,649
-Thank you so much, doc.
-Okay, I have to go now.

228
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:38,484
I have to attend to my other patients.

229
00:13:42,821 --> 00:13:44,240
[sighs]

230
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,659
-[man] Gov, how is the congressman?
-[nurse] Hold on. You can't go there.

231
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:47,993
Hold on. Why are those people here?

232
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:50,371
Diego, Arnaldo.

233
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:54,500
Stop. We have to accommodate them.

234
00:13:55,292 --> 00:14:00,297
Now is the best time
to get the sympathy of the public.

235
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:02,383
Now, you two, be nice.

236
00:14:03,175 --> 00:14:06,345
Come. We're ready. Stay here, Diego.

237
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:08,472
[reporter] What happened
to the congressman?

238
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:09,890
[speaker id] He had a heart attack.

239
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:12,309
He is in a very critical condition now.

240
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:16,522
He's going to be transferred
to Manila for his surgery.

241
00:14:16,605 --> 00:14:18,607
[reporter] What caused the heart attack?

242
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:23,362
[ominous music playing]

243
00:14:51,432 --> 00:14:54,435
[tense music playing]

244
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:06,196
<i>Should I put an end</i>
<i>to your suffering, Julio?</i>

245
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:11,160
<i>Just say the word…</i>

246
00:15:11,702 --> 00:15:16,290
<i>And I'll remove the tubes</i>
<i>keeping you alive, one by one.</i>

247
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:25,507
[tense music swelling]

248
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:39,605
What caused the heart attack?

249
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:43,400
Everyone knows our family is
going through a lot of stress.

250
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:45,527
You know the congressman.

251
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:49,782
Even when his reputation
was being questioned,

252
00:15:49,865 --> 00:15:53,202
he kept on working to make sure
that Poblacion Ardiente is safe.

253
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:24,984
[nurse] Hi, ma'am. Excuse me.

254
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:27,736
You have to leave the room

255
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:30,823
so we can prepare
the congressman for transport.

256
00:16:37,496 --> 00:16:40,040
[tense music playing]

257
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:13,490
Ma'am, who do you think
is attacking your family?

258
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:15,701
-We're still investigating.
-[clears throat]

259
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:18,662
[Arnaldo] But I want to assure
the people of Poblacion Ardiente

260
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:21,248
that, while the congressman is resting,

261
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:25,044
his undying service
to this town will continue.

262
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,504
I will personally
take care of his affairs.

263
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:28,714
[clears throat]

264
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:32,134
Honestly, now is not the best
time to talk about politics.

265
00:17:32,217 --> 00:17:34,928
What's important is the
congressman's speedy recovery, right?

266
00:17:35,554 --> 00:17:38,932
So, to our supporters
in Poblacion Ardiente,

267
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:41,685
we need your prayers
for the speedy recovery

268
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:43,812
of our beloved congressman.

269
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,189
Governor, one more question!

270
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:49,193
Um, enough, enough.
That is all. Thank you.

271
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,697
Diego, Arnaldo.

272
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:54,782
-Gov.
-Ivy.

273
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:56,325
Emilia.

274
00:17:56,408 --> 00:18:00,287
I'll go ahead to give
your family some privacy.

275
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:02,414
Thank you for your time.

276
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:04,625
Of course.

277
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:07,419
Ivy, thank you
for your concern. I appreciate it.

278
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:09,296
It's nothing, Mr. Mayor.

279
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:13,509
I'm on my way out too.
Would you like to ride with me?

280
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:16,261
No, it's okay, Emilia.
I brought my car with me.

281
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,680
Arnaldo, coordinate with the doctor, okay?

282
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:21,141
I still have a lot to take care of.

283
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,769
Ivy, I'll take you home.

284
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:27,940
Arnaldo, you'll be coordinating
with the doctor, remember?

285
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:32,111
Diego, you see Ivy home.

286
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,113
Why me?

287
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:38,158
Diego, I said bring Ivy home.

288
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:40,744
Make sure nothing bad happens to her,

289
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:42,204
or else you'll answer to me.

290
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:44,456
Ivy, I'll go ahead.

291
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:49,044
Arnaldo, take care of your grandfather.

292
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:52,673
Diego, bring Ivy home.

293
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:58,470
[tense music playing]

294
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:02,808
Keep her safe.

295
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:08,230
Our enemies know she's on our side.
I don't want her to get involved.

296
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:16,488
Ivy.

297
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:19,116
[tense music playing]

298
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:29,751
Let's go.

299
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:59,823
Maybe now you have an answer
to my question earlier.

300
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,288
What question?

301
00:20:06,371 --> 00:20:08,916
What do you want from my family?

302
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:12,169
I know what you're doing.
You're toying with my mom and brother.

303
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:17,507
Mr. Torillo, I can see
that you don't like me.

304
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:23,180
But I hope despite that,
you won't judge me.

305
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:28,018
Because you don't know who I am
and what I'm going through.

306
00:20:28,101 --> 00:20:31,188
[quiet music playing]

307
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:37,152
Well, maybe that's the problem.
I don't know you.

308
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:42,032
Who are you, Ms. Aguas?

309
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:45,452
What do you want from my family?
What do you want from this town?

310
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:49,289
Ever since you arrived,
bad things started happening.

311
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:55,587
So? Answer my question.
Who are you, Ms. Aguas?

312
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:00,509
You know what? Just stop the car.

313
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:02,135
Stop the car.

314
00:21:03,011 --> 00:21:04,096
Stop it.

315
00:21:05,555 --> 00:21:06,723
Get down.

316
00:21:11,019 --> 00:21:12,479
I can go home on my own.

317
00:21:12,562 --> 00:21:14,731
Even if you won't answer my question,

318
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:18,151
I'll find out
who you really are, Ms. Aguas.

319
00:21:18,819 --> 00:21:21,488
[car accelerating]

320
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:33,208
[reporter] <i>Why did he have a heart attack?</i>

321
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:37,587
<i>Everyone knows our family is</i>
<i>going through a lot of stress.</i>

322
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:39,423
<i>You know the congressman.</i>

323
00:21:39,506 --> 00:21:42,050
<i>Even when his reputation</i>
<i>was being questioned,</i>

324
00:21:42,134 --> 00:21:43,760
<i>he kept on working.</i>

325
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:46,847
[ominous music playing]

326
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:49,766
[door opens]

327
00:22:01,194 --> 00:22:02,404
Emilia, why did you do it?

328
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,365
Why did you cover up for me?

329
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:09,286
Do you want your sons to know
what you did to their grandfather?

330
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:14,750
I will keep everything a secret
if you do what I want.

331
00:22:15,334 --> 00:22:19,379
You know, Emilia, if you think
you can keep me on a leash,

332
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:22,466
then you're wrong.
I won't let you do that.

333
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:23,925
On the contrary, I don't want you here.

334
00:22:24,634 --> 00:22:27,429
If you want, you can stay with
your relatives, if you still have any.

335
00:22:29,347 --> 00:22:32,059
Honestly, you'll only get
in the way of my plans.

336
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:34,728
What's your plan?
What are you really up to?

337
00:22:34,811 --> 00:22:37,105
You don't have to know
because you're not part of it.

338
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,441
Come, we have a meeting with the family.

339
00:22:41,777 --> 00:22:43,111
[sighs]

340
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,950
Good, you're both here.

341
00:22:50,327 --> 00:22:53,246
Diego, how was your ride with Ivy?

342
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:54,956
[tense music playing]

343
00:23:06,426 --> 00:23:08,887
I know you're worried
about your grandfather.

344
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:14,684
But this is not the right time
to be emotional.

345
00:23:15,310 --> 00:23:18,605
We need to hold the fort
while your grandpa is sick.

346
00:23:18,688 --> 00:23:22,359
Arnaldo, you will go with him to Manila.

347
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:25,946
Ma, I'm the mayor here.
I can't just leave.

348
00:23:26,029 --> 00:23:28,490
I've been a mayor before. I'll handle it.

349
00:23:29,366 --> 00:23:32,619
I can't leave this place because
your grandpa's responsibilities

350
00:23:32,702 --> 00:23:35,122
as a congressman fall on me.

351
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:39,000
And you're the only one I can trust
to take care of your grandfather.

352
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:44,381
He's more important to you
than being a mayor, right?

353
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:48,426
Son, we have to be united in our decision.

354
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:50,137
We need to show the people
that we're strong.

355
00:23:51,721 --> 00:23:53,849
So, when your grandfather gets better,

356
00:23:53,932 --> 00:23:57,602
he will come back to a strong
and orderly Ardiente.

357
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:00,647
I am now the matriarch of this family.

358
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:02,858
[ominous music playing]

359
00:24:02,941 --> 00:24:07,487
Son, I need your support.
All your support.

360
00:24:11,491 --> 00:24:14,119
Raul, sit beside me.

361
00:24:22,794 --> 00:24:24,921
Bring the food!

362
00:24:52,324 --> 00:24:55,327
[ominous music playing]

363
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:17,265
[Emilia] <i>My time has come.</i>

364
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:21,436
<i>Now that the king is gone…</i>

365
00:25:25,065 --> 00:25:26,524
<i>I shall reign as queen.</i>

366
00:25:31,238 --> 00:25:33,323
Arnaldo, is the ambulance
that's going to take

367
00:25:33,406 --> 00:25:35,700
your grandfather to Manila ready?

368
00:25:36,284 --> 00:25:38,411
-I've taken care of it.
-Good.

369
00:25:38,495 --> 00:25:40,538
Diego, do you have
your grandfather's things?

370
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:44,042
-Yes, Mom. Everything's in here.
-Okay.

371
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:49,881
Governor,

372
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:53,927
the congressman's supporters
have gathered outside the hospital.

373
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:57,222
Okay. Good. Let's go.

374
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:59,849
Ma'am, where's Mr. Raul?

375
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:02,435
We need your complete family to be there.

376
00:26:03,019 --> 00:26:04,729
It's for the press release photo.

377
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:08,817
He can't make it.
He's working on a business transaction.

378
00:26:08,900 --> 00:26:10,026
Let's go.

379
00:26:11,361 --> 00:26:14,364
[slow instrumental playing]

380
00:26:58,450 --> 00:26:59,993
[young Ivy] <i>Hey, don't jump!</i>

381
00:27:00,076 --> 00:27:03,455
-Hey! Grab my hand! Hurry!
-[shouting]

382
00:27:04,372 --> 00:27:05,999
<i>You're hurt.</i>

383
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:09,127
[young Diego] <i>Thank you.</i>

384
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:17,552
<i>Lily, thanks for helping me out.</i>

385
00:27:25,685 --> 00:27:28,229
Stay away from us!
We don't need your help.

386
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:31,274
Mr. Torillo, I'm here
because I want to help.

387
00:27:31,358 --> 00:27:34,361
You want to help? Then leave Ardiente!

388
00:27:35,570 --> 00:27:37,030
Who are you, Ms. Aguas?

389
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:40,450
What do you want from my family?
What do you want from this town?

390
00:27:41,201 --> 00:27:43,328
Ever since you arrived,
bad things started happening.

391
00:27:49,042 --> 00:27:52,879
[thinking] <i>You've changed.</i>
<i>But I've changed too.</i>

392
00:27:54,005 --> 00:27:58,635
<i>There's no point telling you</i>
<i>that I'm Lily.</i>

393
00:27:59,427 --> 00:28:02,430
[slow instrumental playing]

394
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:25,537
<i>You shouldn't get dragged</i>
<i>into this, Diego.</i>

395
00:28:25,620 --> 00:28:28,915
<i>But if you get in my way…</i>

396
00:28:28,998 --> 00:28:31,876
<i>I have no choice</i>
<i>but to deal with you too.</i>

397
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:38,007
[woman crying] Congressman.

398
00:28:39,926 --> 00:28:41,386
Congressman.

399
00:28:41,469 --> 00:28:43,805
[sobbing]

400
00:28:43,888 --> 00:28:47,142
Congressman. Poor congressman.

401
00:28:49,144 --> 00:28:51,521
Congressman, get well soon.

402
00:28:51,604 --> 00:28:54,399
[woman] We'll pray for you, Congressman!

403
00:28:54,482 --> 00:28:57,152
-We love you, Congressman!
-Get well soon, Congressman!

404
00:28:57,235 --> 00:28:58,737
We love you, Congressman!

405
00:28:58,820 --> 00:29:00,572
Long live, Congressman Ardiente!

406
00:29:00,655 --> 00:29:02,365
[townsfolk] Long live!

407
00:29:02,449 --> 00:29:04,159
-Viva Ardiente!
-[townsfolk] Viva Ardiente!

408
00:29:04,242 --> 00:29:07,120
-[man] Viva Ardiente!
-[townsfolk] Viva Ardiente!

409
00:29:07,203 --> 00:29:10,290
-[man] Viva Ardiente!
-[townsfolk] Viva Ardiente!

410
00:29:10,373 --> 00:29:13,168
-[man] Viva Ardiente!
-[townsfolk] Viva Ardiente!

411
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:14,711
Hold on.

412
00:29:15,712 --> 00:29:18,173
[man] Long live, Congressman Ardiente!

413
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:19,215
[townsfolk] Long live!

414
00:29:19,299 --> 00:29:21,468
-[man] Viva Ardiente!
-[townsfolk] Viva Ardiente!

415
00:29:22,510 --> 00:29:24,387
-Ivy.
-Emilia.

416
00:29:24,471 --> 00:29:27,140
I'm glad you're here.

417
00:29:29,309 --> 00:29:31,269
The people really love the congressman.

418
00:29:31,352 --> 00:29:33,271
They really do, Ivy.

419
00:29:33,354 --> 00:29:35,857
They'll support the Ardientes forever.

420
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:38,485
Hey, come. Join us for a picture.

421
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:40,862
-No, no. It's okay. I'm fine.
-No, Ivy.

422
00:29:40,945 --> 00:29:44,324
Since you're one
of our supporters, you should join us!

423
00:29:44,407 --> 00:29:46,242
Arnaldo, Diego, it's time for the picture.

424
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:49,537
Let's stand here by the ambulance.

425
00:29:49,621 --> 00:29:52,499
Diego, Arnaldo, picture!

426
00:29:57,003 --> 00:29:59,088
[tense music playing]

427
00:30:03,092 --> 00:30:05,804
Include the ambulance, please.

428
00:30:37,877 --> 00:30:40,922
-Mom, I'll head to Manila.
-Stay safe there.

429
00:30:41,005 --> 00:30:43,341
Take good care of your grandfather.

430
00:30:43,424 --> 00:30:45,844
Okay, I'll be back
as soon grandpa's settled.

431
00:30:45,927 --> 00:30:47,846
Okay. Keep me posted.

432
00:30:49,931 --> 00:30:52,183
-Ivy.
-Take care, Mr. Mayor.

433
00:30:56,896 --> 00:30:58,231
You don't have to come with me.

434
00:30:58,857 --> 00:31:00,275
But I want you to do something.

435
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:03,194
-[Jepoy] What is it, Mayor?
-Look after Ms. Aguas.

436
00:31:05,238 --> 00:31:07,448
Protect her at all times.

437
00:31:09,450 --> 00:31:12,745
If I may ask, Mayor,
do you like Ms. Aguas?

438
00:31:14,205 --> 00:31:16,332
You already know the answer, Madrigal.

439
00:31:17,709 --> 00:31:20,253
And you know
that I always get what I want.

440
00:31:21,004 --> 00:31:22,422
I'll go now.

441
00:31:23,464 --> 00:31:24,591
Let's go.

442
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:26,426
[soft crying]

443
00:31:26,509 --> 00:31:31,764
[townsfolk chanting] Ardiente!
Ardiente! Ardiente!

444
00:31:31,848 --> 00:31:36,394
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

445
00:31:36,477 --> 00:31:43,151
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

446
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:52,744
Auntie.

447
00:31:54,162 --> 00:31:56,497
-What's with all the bags?
-Uh…

448
00:31:57,457 --> 00:32:01,586
Wait. What happened?
Did you finally leave them?

449
00:32:01,669 --> 00:32:02,879
No, I didn't.

450
00:32:02,962 --> 00:32:05,131
Does your wife know you're here?

451
00:32:05,214 --> 00:32:07,842
-She might do something to us!
-Auntie, relax.

452
00:32:07,926 --> 00:32:10,553
Emilia thinks I'm with my relatives.

453
00:32:10,637 --> 00:32:14,057
But she doesn't know I'm here.

454
00:32:14,140 --> 00:32:16,768
Why? What happened?

455
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:20,813
It's a long story.

456
00:32:21,814 --> 00:32:24,150
As much as possible,
I don't want to talk about it.

457
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:26,527
I don't want to think about it.

458
00:32:26,611 --> 00:32:29,197
And it's better that
you don't know the reason.

459
00:32:29,906 --> 00:32:32,283
How are you? How is she?

460
00:32:32,825 --> 00:32:35,536
Her condition didn't improve.
She's still the same.

461
00:32:36,287 --> 00:32:38,581
Maybe it's better she stays that way.

462
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:41,459
It's better that
she can't remember anything.

463
00:32:43,211 --> 00:32:44,921
-Come inside, get some rest.
-Okay.

464
00:32:45,004 --> 00:32:48,007
[quiet music playing]

465
00:32:56,891 --> 00:32:58,476
[Belen] Just leave your things here.

466
00:33:04,899 --> 00:33:06,275
She's in there.

467
00:33:07,026 --> 00:33:08,528
Thanks.

468
00:33:13,157 --> 00:33:14,117
[Raul] Love…

469
00:33:15,868 --> 00:33:17,328
I'm back.

470
00:33:19,288 --> 00:33:22,291
[tense music playing]

471
00:34:04,459 --> 00:34:06,419
Love, do you want to catch
some fresh air outside?

472
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:12,258
Come on.

473
00:34:12,341 --> 00:34:15,011
[bleak instrumental playing]

474
00:34:23,644 --> 00:34:25,813
Now that… [clears throat]

475
00:34:27,523 --> 00:34:29,067
your grandfather's recovering…

476
00:34:30,234 --> 00:34:31,819
uh…

477
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:35,490
will they still push through
with their project?

478
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:43,956
I think it'll take some time
before they do.

479
00:34:44,832 --> 00:34:48,878
Grandpa's office is the one leading it.

480
00:34:49,378 --> 00:34:52,215
[somber music playing]

481
00:34:54,884 --> 00:34:58,721
It's not right to celebrate your
grandfather's condition,

482
00:34:58,805 --> 00:34:59,847
but…

483
00:35:01,307 --> 00:35:08,272
it's good news for everyone
that the project was halted.

484
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:25,039
Ivy, thank you so much
for your time. Sorry, short notice.

485
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:27,416
Oh, come on, anytime.
What's this for anyway?

486
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:31,003
You'll know soon enough. Hi, everyone!

487
00:35:31,087 --> 00:35:33,047
Arnaldo, why are you here?

488
00:35:33,131 --> 00:35:34,841
Didn't I tell you I'd be back right away?

489
00:35:34,924 --> 00:35:36,425
-Hi, Ivy.
-Mr. Mayor.

490
00:35:36,509 --> 00:35:37,802
-Okay.
-What's this meeting about?

491
00:35:37,885 --> 00:35:41,055
Let's start the meeting.
Everyone, this is Ms. Ivy Aguas.

492
00:35:41,139 --> 00:35:45,476
I'm sure you already
know Ivy, so let's cut to the chase.

493
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:47,562
Everyone, this is Ms. Ivy Aguas,

494
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:49,564
our investor for the EPZ Project.

495
00:35:49,647 --> 00:35:52,108
[applause]

496
00:35:54,735 --> 00:35:55,862
And tomorrow,

497
00:35:55,945 --> 00:35:58,823
she'll be coming with us
for the groundbreaking ceremony.

498
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:01,742
Groundbreaking?

499
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:05,580
Yes. Ivy's going ahead
with her investment.

500
00:36:05,663 --> 00:36:07,123
I hadn't mentioned it.

501
00:36:07,206 --> 00:36:10,459
In fact, I'm having our press
releases prepared by tomorrow.

502
00:36:10,543 --> 00:36:13,045
[tense music playing]

503
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,300
Excuse us. Emilia.

504
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:22,722
What about our problem with the farmers?

505
00:36:27,018 --> 00:36:30,521
Ivy, there is nothing to fix.

506
00:36:30,605 --> 00:36:35,067
For progress to take effect,
someone should make sacrifices.

507
00:36:35,151 --> 00:36:37,069
You know about that, right?

508
00:36:40,448 --> 00:36:43,534
I'm sorry, but those farmers
need to evacuate that land

509
00:36:43,618 --> 00:36:44,994
as soon as possible.

510
00:36:45,786 --> 00:36:47,121
You know, Ivy?

511
00:36:47,205 --> 00:36:50,374
This project will
push through, no matter what,

512
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:52,627
especially now I'm in charge of it.

513
00:36:52,710 --> 00:36:57,381
And all your plans for this project
will finally come true.

514
00:36:57,465 --> 00:37:00,718
[tense music playing]

515
00:37:03,971 --> 00:37:06,974
Is there something wrong?
You look bothered, Ivy.

516
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:10,061
[tense music continues]

517
00:37:10,645 --> 00:37:14,857
The Ardientes truly can't
accept no for an answer,

518
00:37:14,941 --> 00:37:16,651
can they, Emilia?

519
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:20,196
But as I said,

520
00:37:20,279 --> 00:37:23,199
I will not push through with my investment

521
00:37:24,242 --> 00:37:26,744
if it will inconvenience the farmers.

522
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:32,500
Ivy, tell me.

523
00:37:33,459 --> 00:37:35,336
Why is this so personal to you?

524
00:37:36,712 --> 00:37:39,048
Is there something you want to reveal?

525
00:37:39,131 --> 00:37:41,008
Like skeletons in the closet?

526
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:44,387
Dark past? Dirty laundry?

527
00:37:46,138 --> 00:37:47,640
Or maybe…

528
00:37:49,475 --> 00:37:52,895
you have relatives who are farmers?

529
00:37:55,314 --> 00:37:58,359
You know, Ivy, as a good businesswoman,

530
00:37:58,442 --> 00:38:01,821
you should learn how
to set aside cheap sentiments

531
00:38:01,904 --> 00:38:04,699
over million-dollar projects.

532
00:38:07,994 --> 00:38:09,704
Excuse me.

533
00:38:10,371 --> 00:38:11,330
[Emilia] Okay.

534
00:38:15,251 --> 00:38:16,419
Let's resume the meeting.

535
00:38:17,586 --> 00:38:19,088
Give me the folder, please.

536
00:38:19,171 --> 00:38:21,299
Arnaldo, would you like to join us?

537
00:38:24,343 --> 00:38:28,889
I thought now that Julio is
out of the game,

538
00:38:29,598 --> 00:38:32,852
it'd be easier for me
to tear down the Ardientes.

539
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:36,230
Julio is sly.

540
00:38:37,189 --> 00:38:39,900
But Emilia's desperate for power.

541
00:38:39,984 --> 00:38:42,695
[dramatic music playing]

542
00:38:48,784 --> 00:38:51,746
You can end Emilia Ardiente
any time you want.

543
00:38:54,790 --> 00:38:57,209
So we can go back to our normal lives.

544
00:39:00,629 --> 00:39:01,797
Our simple lives.

545
00:39:09,805 --> 00:39:10,765
I wish.

546
00:39:11,515 --> 00:39:13,601
If only it were that easy, Jepoy.

547
00:39:14,518 --> 00:39:18,773
I wish it were easy to heal the
pain that's dragging me down.

548
00:39:19,398 --> 00:39:21,108
But as time goes by,

549
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:24,904
it hurts even more, it feels heavier.

550
00:39:24,987 --> 00:39:26,614
Like I want to explode.

551
00:39:27,782 --> 00:39:29,116
But this kind of anger…

552
00:39:30,993 --> 00:39:34,830
it can only be tamed
once justice is served.

553
00:39:35,414 --> 00:39:36,749
Only justice can take it away.

554
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:42,088
So, it's not that simple.

555
00:39:43,047 --> 00:39:44,799
[tense music playing]

556
00:39:58,270 --> 00:40:01,440
<i>I have to be more careful with my plans.</i>

557
00:40:01,524 --> 00:40:03,567
<i>Now that Emilia got what she wanted…</i>

558
00:40:04,944 --> 00:40:07,655
<i>to be the queen of this town…</i>

559
00:40:07,738 --> 00:40:13,577
<i>I will be the hindrance to her ambition.</i>

560
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:23,712
<i>I'll make sure you won't last</i>
<i>long on your throne,</i>

561
00:40:23,796 --> 00:40:26,924
<i>Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

562
00:40:33,347 --> 00:40:36,642
Raul, looks like you
really prepared for this.

563
00:40:36,725 --> 00:40:38,102
[Raul chuckles]

564
00:40:38,185 --> 00:40:40,438
Anyway, I still have lots to do inside.

565
00:40:40,521 --> 00:40:41,772
All right. Sure you don't want any?

566
00:40:41,856 --> 00:40:43,232
-I'm good.
-[Raul chuckles]

567
00:40:43,315 --> 00:40:45,484
-I'll leave some for you then.
-Mm-hmm.

568
00:40:58,038 --> 00:40:59,665
Let's give this a try.

569
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:05,629
Love.

570
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:10,593
I'm sorry it took me so long
to spend time with you like this.

571
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:12,219
You know how it is.

572
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:15,014
I've gotten really busy back home.

573
00:41:15,097 --> 00:41:17,057
[quiet music playing]

574
00:41:18,976 --> 00:41:20,686
But you know what?

575
00:41:22,104 --> 00:41:23,856
If I were to choose…

576
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:29,195
I'd rather stay here with you.

577
00:41:31,989 --> 00:41:34,950
I won't go back to the Ardientes.

578
00:41:40,456 --> 00:41:43,459
[somber music playing]

579
00:42:07,316 --> 00:42:08,776
[Emilia] Take that to another room.

580
00:42:13,072 --> 00:42:14,323
What's happening, Ma?

581
00:42:14,406 --> 00:42:17,076
[tense music playing]

582
00:42:17,159 --> 00:42:20,704
From now on, I will be
occupying your grandpa's office,

583
00:42:20,788 --> 00:42:23,123
his conference room, everything.

584
00:42:23,207 --> 00:42:25,918
From leading this town, to the Senate.

585
00:42:26,001 --> 00:42:27,503
You're running for the Senate?
But I'm the one

586
00:42:27,586 --> 00:42:29,964
grandpa's been grooming
to someday take his place.

587
00:42:30,047 --> 00:42:33,175
Arnaldo, someday your time will come.

588
00:42:33,259 --> 00:42:34,927
But now, it is my time.

589
00:42:37,846 --> 00:42:40,474
EMILIA ARDIENTE, GAMBLING LORD?

590
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:44,770
Well, no offense,
you're not the perfect candidate.

591
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:49,149
Your name's already been
tarnished by that scandal.

592
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:51,360
All because of the mess Dad left.

593
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:55,656
Politics is dirty, but for many years

594
00:42:55,739 --> 00:42:58,701
the Ardiente name has stayed clean.

595
00:42:58,784 --> 00:43:00,286
You know why?

596
00:43:01,161 --> 00:43:04,540
Because I'm an expert in
cleaning the dirt from our name.

597
00:43:05,457 --> 00:43:08,836
And while I'm in charge,
no one can ever go against us,

598
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:10,796
no one can ever go against me.

599
00:43:12,339 --> 00:43:13,924
[ominous music playing]

600
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:23,475
You should rest. I'll watch over you.

601
00:43:23,559 --> 00:43:26,645
[ominous music playing]

602
00:43:34,069 --> 00:43:36,071
Someday, you'll understand
why I'm doing this.

603
00:43:37,239 --> 00:43:39,783
Someday, you'll forgive me for this…

604
00:43:40,367 --> 00:43:41,785
Jasmin.

605
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:56,383
Emilia's something else.

606
00:43:56,467 --> 00:43:58,677
I bet she'd even have
Satan himself killed.

607
00:44:07,394 --> 00:44:11,023
[thunder rumbling]

608
00:44:17,404 --> 00:44:20,032
[tense music playing]

609
00:44:22,326 --> 00:44:23,952
[thunder rumbling]

610
00:44:34,296 --> 00:44:36,298
[thunder rumbling]

611
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:42,346
Camia?

612
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:48,852
[grunts]

613
00:44:55,734 --> 00:44:57,945
<i>Camia, hang on.</i>

614
00:44:58,028 --> 00:45:01,031
[tense music playing]

615
00:45:03,283 --> 00:45:05,077
THANK YOU GOVERNOR ARDIENTE
WE LOVE YOU!

616
00:45:08,664 --> 00:45:10,499
THANK YOU!
MAYOR EMILIA ARDIENTE

617
00:45:23,720 --> 00:45:25,013
Raul? Raul?

618
00:45:25,097 --> 00:45:27,266
Auntie. Auntie, I'll carry her.

619
00:45:27,349 --> 00:45:29,685
-What happened?
-Let's go. Just help me get her inside.

620
00:45:29,768 --> 00:45:32,438
Come on. Let's take her inside. Hurry.

621
00:45:35,065 --> 00:45:38,235
All right. It's okay, Auntie.

622
00:45:38,318 --> 00:45:40,028
Who is she?

623
00:45:40,988 --> 00:45:43,115
Her name's Jasmin.

624
00:45:43,198 --> 00:45:44,158
Jasmin?

625
00:45:44,241 --> 00:45:45,909
[quiet music playing]

626
00:45:56,253 --> 00:45:58,130
They may have killed Camia…

627
00:45:59,506 --> 00:46:01,467
but I brought you back as Jasmin.

628
00:46:02,259 --> 00:46:05,804
We'll use that against
the Ardientes someday.

629
00:46:06,638 --> 00:46:10,642
But all this time,
you've been my reason to live.

630
00:46:12,102 --> 00:46:15,314
You bring back my soul
that's slowly been dying

631
00:46:15,397 --> 00:46:17,441
in the hands of the Ardientes.

632
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:24,031
[phone ringing]

633
00:46:28,785 --> 00:46:30,329
-Hello?
-<i>Hello, Raul?</i>

634
00:46:30,412 --> 00:46:31,747
Play time is over.

635
00:46:31,830 --> 00:46:32,789
Come back here.

636
00:46:33,707 --> 00:46:34,708
Really, Emilia?

637
00:46:34,791 --> 00:46:38,462
After kicking me out
for what I did to your father,

638
00:46:38,545 --> 00:46:40,964
you want me to go back?
Do you think I'm stupid?

639
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:43,550
<i>Will you send your men after me</i>
<i>if I don't return?</i>

640
00:46:43,634 --> 00:46:44,843
And what's this for?

641
00:46:44,927 --> 00:46:46,303
[sighs]

642
00:46:46,386 --> 00:46:50,974
Oh, I know. You want me to act fake
for the press again.

643
00:46:51,058 --> 00:46:55,187
Emilia, I want you to know that I'm sick
of everything you're doing.

644
00:46:55,270 --> 00:46:56,188
<i>Raul.</i>

645
00:46:56,271 --> 00:46:58,732
Did some bad air pollute your brain?

646
00:46:58,815 --> 00:47:00,859
<i>Wherever you might be right now,</i>

647
00:47:00,943 --> 00:47:03,237
it's turning you crazy again.

648
00:47:03,820 --> 00:47:06,031
You know, now that Papa's not around,

649
00:47:06,114 --> 00:47:07,991
I'm in charge. Me.

650
00:47:08,742 --> 00:47:14,039
I can find you wherever you're hiding
with your dirty tramp.

651
00:47:14,122 --> 00:47:16,375
<i>Now, if you don't want to be</i>
<i>added to my list of trophies</i>

652
00:47:16,458 --> 00:47:20,295
with your filthy hooker,
you'll be home here tomorrow.

653
00:47:21,463 --> 00:47:22,965
[sighs]

654
00:47:23,799 --> 00:47:24,967
[exhales]

655
00:47:28,053 --> 00:47:32,558
Auntie, please take care of Jasmin.

656
00:47:32,641 --> 00:47:34,142
I have to go home.

657
00:47:34,226 --> 00:47:37,187
Look at how the Ardientes
destroyed your life,

658
00:47:37,896 --> 00:47:39,815
like what they did to my brother
when he was alive.

659
00:47:39,898 --> 00:47:41,858
When will you leave that life behind?

660
00:47:41,942 --> 00:47:46,738
Auntie, I'll be free from the
Ardientes soon, but not right now.

661
00:47:46,822 --> 00:47:49,241
How do you think your wife
will take it if she finds out

662
00:47:49,324 --> 00:47:53,495
you're keeping a woman here?
We don't even know her!

663
00:47:54,830 --> 00:47:55,664
Auntie.

664
00:47:55,747 --> 00:47:58,834
It's not that I'm complaining,
but when you brought her here,

665
00:47:58,917 --> 00:48:02,462
you said we'd just help her recover.

666
00:48:02,546 --> 00:48:04,464
Then we'd take her back to her family.

667
00:48:04,548 --> 00:48:07,050
Auntie, she doesn't have a family anymore.

668
00:48:07,134 --> 00:48:10,095
We can't just leave Ca--

669
00:48:11,847 --> 00:48:13,890
We can't just leave Jasmin.

670
00:48:13,974 --> 00:48:15,976
You need to tell the truth.

671
00:48:16,059 --> 00:48:19,771
If Emilia finds out
you're keeping a woman here,

672
00:48:20,272 --> 00:48:23,483
she won't just have your head,
she'll have Jasmin's too.

673
00:48:25,861 --> 00:48:27,613
[tense music playing]

674
00:48:36,788 --> 00:48:38,582
[Emilia] <i>Can you look for my husband?</i>

675
00:48:38,665 --> 00:48:41,543
<i>A queen can't show up</i>
<i>without her king now, can she?</i>

676
00:48:41,627 --> 00:48:43,920
[Ivy] <i>You're so happy right now, Emilia.</i>

677
00:48:44,004 --> 00:48:45,422
<i>Enjoy it while it lasts.</i>

678
00:48:45,964 --> 00:48:50,302
<i>I see that you're still siding</i>
<i>with the Ardientes, Senator.</i>

679
00:48:50,385 --> 00:48:52,095
<i>What's your game, Ms. Aguas?</i>

680
00:48:52,179 --> 00:48:53,305
<i>If I tell you,</i>

681
00:48:53,388 --> 00:48:55,557
<i>you might not want</i>
<i>to play anymore, Senator.</i>

682
00:48:55,641 --> 00:48:59,353
[Belen] <i>It's Jasmin. She's gone.</i>
<i>I've searched the whole house for her.</i>

683
00:48:59,436 --> 00:49:02,648
<i>Auntie, didn't I say to keep</i>
<i>an eye on her at all times?</i>

684
00:49:02,731 --> 00:49:06,026
[Ivy] <i>Hi, Mr. Torillo. You look tense.</i>

685
00:49:06,109 --> 00:49:09,071
[theme music playing]
